{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":64345820,"ns":0,"title":"Anderson acceleration","extract":"In mathematics, Anderson acceleration, also called Anderson mixing, is a method for the acceleration of the convergence rate of fixed-point iterations. Introduced by Donald G. Anderson, this technique can be used to find the solution to fixed point equations \n  \n    \n      \n        f\n        (\n        x\n        )\n        =\n        x\n      \n    \n    {\\displaystyle f(x)=x}\n  \n often arising in the field of computational science.","description":"Iterative method in numerical analysis","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}